  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Stonex Financial recorded $922M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Stonex Financial won 276 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.3M. Stonex Financial obligations are down 30.7% year over year. Stonex Financial has moved through several cycles since FY21, when obligations were $1.1B, rising to $1.7B in FY22 and remaining $1.7B in FY23, then falling to $703M in FY24 before recovering to $1.3B in FY25 and arriving at $922M in FY26 year to date. Stonex Financial current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the reported figures are contract obligations except for award-value tables not shown here. Stonex Financial performance this year should be read in the context of the multi-year pattern: obligations peaked in FY22 and FY23 at $1.7B, dropped in FY24 to $703M, rebounded in FY25 to $1.3B, and stand at $922M so far in FY26. The count, average award size, and year-over-year change summarize activity through the fiscal year to date.",
